Run the NFS driver's qemu-img info as the service user

NfsDriver._qemu_img_info is the driver's one forced-root call. It
passes run_as_root=True to _qemu_img_info_base in
cinder/volume/drivers/remotefs.py, which bypasses that method's
"run_as_root = run_as_root or self._execute_as_root" line. Every
other file operation of the driver follows nas_secure_file_operations
through that line (_execute_as_root is True by constructor default).

Upstream forced root in commit dbc9c7ca59 (2017) so that the driver
could still read files a Nova instance had attached and the cinder
user could not open. Under the restricted posture of #979 decision
D3 there is no root to fall back to: sudo has no sudoers entry for
the service user, and every file is owned by that user anyway.
Without this change every operation that inspects an image format
fails (spike #985, evidence part 1, section (a.4)).

The flip is necessary but not sufficient. With run_as_root=False the
"or" resolves to self._execute_as_root, which RemoteFSDriver.__init__
leaves True; only NfsDriver.set_nas_security_options clears it, and
only when nas_secure_file_operations resolves to true. That option
defaults to auto, which resolves to true only for a new install able
to write .cinderSecureEnvIndicator onto the share and to false for
every existing one. The cinder-operator (#987) therefore has to set
nas_secure_file_operations = true explicitly rather than rely on the
default; without it this call still runs through `sudo
cinder-rootwrap`, which has no sudoers entry, and every
create-from-image, clone and extend fails.
tests/container-images/verify_cinder.sh asserts both halves against
the built image: the call resolves to run_as_root=False once
_execute_as_root is False, and to run_as_root=True on the constructor
default.

test_copy_volume_from_snapshot in
cinder/tests/unit/volume/drivers/test_nfs.py keeps expecting
run_as_root=True on image_utils.qemu_img_info and stays green: the
test driver never calls set_nas_security_options, so
_execute_as_root keeps its constructor default True and the or
yields True. The patch therefore carries no test hunk.

Applies to cinder 27.0.0 (2025.2).

Upstream status: not yet proposed.

diff --git a/cinder/volume/drivers/nfs.py b/cinder/volume/drivers/nfs.py
index e07f57c..e5454a5 100644
--- a/cinder/volume/drivers/nfs.py
+++ b/cinder/volume/drivers/nfs.py
@@ -587,7 +587,7 @@ class NfsDriver(remotefs.RemoteFSSnapDriverDistributed):
             volume_name,
             self.configuration.nfs_mount_point_base,
             force_share=True,
-            run_as_root=True)
+            run_as_root=False)
 
     def _check_snapshot_support(self, setup_checking=False):
         """Ensure snapshot support is enabled in config."""
